Z||000014||WhiteFieroBlur||11-22-2001||06:33 PM||||hey no one has said how to install these  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I want details and I wanna know, and I wanted them yesterday  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> well I just been wonderin about putting these on and I want it to be my next project with clear lights. Oh and speaking my lights, how do you get the clear front parking lights? details too please  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000015||SLAMMED87GT||11-22-2001||06:55 PM||||To answer Whiteblur about the clear parking<BR>lights-<P>Clear front lights are actually pretty simple. Like the picture on the top of <BR>Jaei Sun's blue GT, I did the same thing. They lights are actually from an '80s Cadillac and they are the back-up lights!<P>They are very close to the same size and will accept the Fiero's bulb housing although you need to toy with it to fit.<P>To install them you do need to drill some holes in them to fit the Fiero. Just measure the correct length and drill them. The end product is very cool!<P>You can use stock amber bulbs but if you are going for the new look just get Super-Whites! I bought APC Super Whites that are actually a blue bulb. They look great at night!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero10-01,4.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pfierosig_2.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>3" Drop, 17" Primax 618s/Nitto540 205/40, 4" Monza exhaust, Mudstain decklid scoop, 7" wing stands, Clear front and rear lights, custom interior, all options...that's all hehe.||||reg||1
Z||000016||edbone||11-22-2001||10:47 PM||||Well Believe it or not, The mesh is actually-------------Gutter guard from your nearest home improvement store <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Like Lowes or Home depot. To install them is a little tricky though. I took a piece of card board first and made templates of an exact fit. Than I transfered the template onto the guard leaving tabs on each piece. I positioned them into place and screwed them into the plastic through the tabs. Then bend them down into position. But be carefull, it will scratch your paint becuase the edges are sharp. Im looking for a simular mesh but in plastic so as not to scratch.Iv also done my rear lights too||||reg||7
